  "chunk": "score as an indicator of overall progress.\n•Conversation log.The full transcript of game outputs and model re-\nsponses is saved for further analysis.\n4 Results\nIn this section, we quantitively discuss the performance of LLMs playingZork.\nIn Section 5, we further discuss the “thinking” and “reasoning” capabilities.\nFigure 1 summarizes the key numerical results. On the left-hand side, the\naverage final score is shown and reveals large differences between the studied\nLLM-based chatbots. First, note that all LLMs did not exceed a score of ap-\nproximately 75 points, far below the required 350 points to finish the game.\nIn other words, a maximum of∼20% progress was achieved, while on aver-\nage less than∼10% of the game was completed. Second, the results suggest\nthat Claude Opus 4.5 outperforms both Gemini 3 and ChatGPT 5.2, indicating\n6\nFigure 1: Left: Average number of points with standard error bars. Right:\nAverage number of moves per game with standard errors bars. (I) denotes the",
